# ShellCheck project configuration - bash-ol-aws-ami-builder
#
# Policy: every ShellCheck code stays ACTIVE project-wide. The canonical B-T2
# severity is `style` (the strictest), enforced on the command line by
# tests/t002_shellcheck.sh (see TESTING.md "Test model" and Part C). This file
# deliberately declares NO global `disable=` - it would weaken the gate
# everywhere. The only exemptions are three narrow, documented, inline
# `# shellcheck disable=`/`source=` directives at the relevant statements.
#
# `external-sources=true` + `source-path=SCRIPTDIR` let ShellCheck FOLLOW the
# harness's `# shellcheck source=lib/...` directives (resolving SC1091 properly
# rather than suppressing it) - this strengthens checking, it does not relax it.
external-sources=true
source-path=SCRIPTDIR
